# Reading Chekhov in Russian: Fat and Thin
subtitle: "Two school friends meet at a Petersburg–Moscow railway station, until one hears the other's rank: Chekhov's «Толстый и тонкий», adapted, read in Russian."
tags: ["russian","chekhov","russian literature","russian reading","толстый и тонкий"]
teaches: ["reading/reading-literature","phrases/formal-register"]
thumb: "band \"Read Chekhov in Russian\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"The flat that I rented in Russian: который in every case","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/131-russian-which-flat.cast"}

